The MIT grant in section 1 does NOT apply to these files. They remain under
CC BY-SA 3.0, and so does anything you derive from them.

Changes made to the original database
-------------------------------------
The files in docs/data/ are modified derivatives, not verbatim copies:

  * Column subsets — each export carries only the columns the app reads.
  * A derived careerG column added to people.csv, summed from Appearances.
  * franchises.csv and franchise_eras.csv are new tables with no counterpart
    in the original, reconstructing each franchise's renames and relocations
    from the per-season Teams rows (see franchises.py).
  * hof.csv contains only inducted members.
  * Line endings normalised to LF.

The source CSVs in data/csv/ are unmodified as distributed by SABR.

Note on redistribution
----------------------
CC BY-SA 3.0 section 4(a) restricts imposing technological measures that would
prevent recipients from exercising the rights it grants. If you redistribute
this data inside a DRM-protected package such as an App Store binary, keep the
dataset separately obtainable under its license. This repository and its
GitHub Pages build already serve that purpose.

This note is a pointer, not legal advice. For anything commercial, contact
SABR at the address above.
